WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.706 --> 00:00:15.674
On Saturday afternoon Tom and Huck pushed open the creaky door of the haunted house.

2
00:00:16.775 --> 00:00:18.096
The house was very quiet.

3
00:00:18.896 --> 00:00:22.179
In the cracks of the stone floor, sickly looking weeds were growing.

4
00:00:23.099 --> 00:00:27.002
The stone fireplace was crumbling, and cobwebs hung from every corner.

5
00:00:27.022 --> 00:00:32.861
"See," whispered Tom, "haunted houses aren't so bad during the day."

6
00:00:33.982 --> 00:00:34.962
Huck only nodded.

7
00:00:35.582 --> 00:00:39.764
The boys left their tools by the fireplace, and Tom led Huck up the stairs.

8
00:00:40.604 --> 00:00:45.306
The stairs were old and rotten in many places, but the boys had no problem climbing them.

9
00:00:46.426 --> 00:00:49.508
The boys searched a closet for hidden treasure but they found nothing.

10
00:00:51.268 --> 00:01:01.032
Huck was getting ready to go down the stairs when Tom hissed, "Shhh Listen!"

11
00:01:01.052 --> 00:01:01.372
"Wh what is it?"

12
00:01:01.392 --> 00:01:01.613
asked Huck.

13
00:01:01.633 --> 00:01:02.954
"Someone's coming," whispered Tom.

14
00:01:03.654 --> 00:01:05.295
The boys looked at each other in fear.

15
00:01:06.036 --> 00:01:07.537
Then they lay flat on the floor.

16
00:01:08.377 --> 00:01:10.519
Each peered through a knothole in the floorboards.

17
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.521
Two men entered the room below.

18
00:01:14.461 --> 00:01:17.063
One was a Spaniard whom the boys had seen around town.

19
00:01:18.304 --> 00:01:20.265
The boys had never seen the other man before.

20
00:01:22.146 --> 00:01:26.569
The men talked in whispers as they entered the house, but once they shut the door, they began

21
00:01:26.609 --> 00:01:27.810
to speak at normal volume.

22
00:01:29.371 --> 00:01:32.878
"It's dangerous," said the ugly unshaven man to the Spaniard.

23
00:01:32.898 --> 00:01:35.720
"Dangerous?" echoed the Spaniard.

24
00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.961
"I don't care.

25
00:01:36.981 --> 00:01:38.342
I want revenge."

26
00:01:39.783 --> 00:01:41.405
The boys began to shake with fear.

27
00:01:42.125 --> 00:01:44.287
The voice of the Spaniard was Injun Joe's!

28
00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:52.394
Tom and Huck were both sure that when Injun Joe said "revenge," he meant he wanted to get

29
00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:53.214
revenge on them.

30
00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:57.137
"I think it's dangerous," argued the other man.

31
00:01:57.157 --> 00:02:01.704
"If you don't want to help," said Injun Joe, "you can wait for me up the river.

32
00:02:02.365 --> 00:02:04.765
I'll do the job, and then we'll be off to Texas."

33
00:02:04.785 --> 00:02:09.267
"I said I was your partner," said the ugly man, "so I'll help.

34
00:02:10.747 --> 00:02:15.549
I just wish we could have done it—" "I know," interrupted Injun Joe.

35
00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:20.630
"Those darn kids were playing right outside the whole day, so we couldn't have left this house without

36
00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:21.210
being seen."

37
00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.491
"Have you got any food in your sack?"

38
00:02:23.911 --> 00:02:24.571
asked the man.

39
00:02:24.591 --> 00:02:25.992
"I'm starving."

40
00:02:27.624 --> 00:02:31.767
Injun Joe pulled some food out of his very large and very heavy sack, and the two men

41
00:02:31.827 --> 00:02:32.327
had lunch.

42
00:02:33.288 --> 00:02:34.309
Then they fell asleep.

43
00:02:35.089 --> 00:02:39.552
Tom and Huck started for the stairs, but the floorboards creaked and moaned with every step.

44
00:02:40.573 --> 00:02:44.476
They worried that the sleeping men would wake up, so they decided to remain upstairs.

45
00:02:46.497 --> 00:02:49.319
Injun Joe woke first, and then he woke his partner.

46
00:02:49.339 --> 00:02:50.760
"It's almost time."

47
00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:54.122
"Okay," said the ugly man with a yawn.

48
00:02:54.142 --> 00:02:56.124
"But shouldn't we hide our loot here?

49
00:02:56.728 --> 00:02:59.910
Six hundred and fifty dollars in silver is a lot to carry."

50
00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.511
"You're right," said Injun Joe.

51
00:03:02.532 --> 00:03:04.132
"Let's bury it deep."

52
00:03:04.973 --> 00:03:09.015
Injun Joe pulled out his knife and began to dig in the dirt under the rotten floorboards.

53
00:03:10.316 --> 00:03:12.657
It wasn't long before Joe's knife struck something.

54
00:03:12.677 --> 00:03:14.138
"What did you hit?"

55
00:03:14.538 --> 00:03:15.359
asked his partner.

56
00:03:15.379 --> 00:03:19.401
"I'm not sure, but I think it's a box," said Injun Joe.

57
00:03:20.622 --> 00:03:24.484
He reached his hand into the box and pulled out a handful of gold coins.

58
00:03:25.456 --> 00:03:29.658
Everyone in the house—the two men and the two boys—stared at the money.

59
00:03:29.678 --> 00:03:33.379
"I saw a pick in the corner by the fireplace.

60
00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:37.441
Let's find out how much there is," said the man excitedly.

61
00:03:38.081 --> 00:03:41.743
He grabbed the boys' pick, and Injun Joe used it to dig up the box.

62
00:03:41.763 --> 00:03:46.285
"There's over ten-thousand dollars here," said Injun Joe.

63
00:03:46.305 --> 00:03:47.685
"We're rich!"

64
00:03:47.705 --> 00:03:51.827
"You won't need to do that other job now," said the other man.

65
00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:57.153
Injun Joe frowned and said, "It isn't just a robbery, it's also revenge.

66
00:03:58.334 --> 00:04:00.215
As soon as we're finished we'll go to Texas."

67
00:04:01.355 --> 00:04:02.796
"Okay," said the man.

68
00:04:02.816 --> 00:04:05.417
"The sooner we get the job done, the better.

69
00:04:06.137 --> 00:04:07.418
Should we bury the money again?"

70
00:04:08.338 --> 00:04:09.719
Injun Joe looked at the pick.

71
00:04:09.739 --> 00:04:11.279
"What's this doing here?

72
00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:13.700
It wasn't here yesterday," he said.

73
00:04:14.861 --> 00:04:18.302
The two men looked at each other, and then Injun Joe pointed to the ceiling.

74
00:04:19.323 --> 00:04:21.584
Right away the boys knew they were going to die.

75
00:04:22.984 --> 00:04:25.647
Injun Joe grabbed his knife and began to climb the stairs.

76
00:04:26.347 --> 00:04:31.172
The boys were sliding across the floor toward the closet when the stairs made a terrible groaning noise.

77
00:04:32.233 --> 00:04:34.735
Then the stairs crashed down in a cloud of dust.

78
00:04:36.416 --> 00:04:37.758
Injun Joe was furious.

79
00:04:38.498 --> 00:04:42.682
When he got up from the collapsed stairs, his partner reminded him it was time to move out.

80
00:04:42.702 --> 00:04:46.285
"We'll be taking the treasure with us," said Injun Joe.

81
00:04:46.305 --> 00:04:48.748
"Naturally," said the man.

82
00:04:49.964 --> 00:04:54.945
"We'll take it to my hiding place and bury it in number two under the cross," said Injun

83
00:04:54.985 --> 00:04:55.986
Joe as they left.

84
00:04:57.306 --> 00:04:59.287
The boys were both happy and sad.

85
00:05:00.207 --> 00:05:05.108
They were happy to be alive but depressed at having lost a chance to get ten-thousand dollars.

86
00:05:05.128 --> 00:05:10.150
"We need to keep an eye out for Injun Joe," said Tom.

87
00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:11.630
Huck agreed.

88
00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:17.492
"If he comes into town, we should follow him to hiding place number two," Tom added.

89
00:05:18.577 --> 00:05:22.153
Then Tom and Huck walked back to town, dreaming of being rich.
